{%- comment -%}
  Store wording rules, applied to merchant HTML at render time.

  Why this exists rather than a find-and-replace on the products themselves:
  the phrases live in product.description, which is Shopify data. Editing it
  needs the Admin API, and this theme deploys with a Theme Access token that is
  theme-files-only (verified: the Admin API returns 401 for it). So the change
  is made where the copy is displayed.

  IMPORTANT — this is a display layer, not a data fix. The product record still
  says "100% nylon", so Shopify admin, the products.json feed, Google Shopping,
  Klaviyo emails and any app reading the description will all still show the old
  wording. Editing the twelve product descriptions in admin is the real fix;
  after that this snippet can be deleted.

  Usage: {% render 'hnl-copy-rules', html: product.description %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign out = html

  # Longest first — "100% premium nylon" must not be left as "premium premium
  # nylon" by an earlier, shorter rule firing on the same text.
  assign out = out | replace: '100% premium nylon', 'premium nylon'
  assign out = out | replace: '100% Premium Nylon', 'Premium Nylon'
  assign out = out | replace: '100% premium Nylon', 'Premium Nylon'
  assign out = out | replace: '100 % premium nylon', 'premium nylon'

  assign out = out | replace: '100% nylon', 'premium nylon'
  assign out = out | replace: '100% Nylon', 'Premium Nylon'
  assign out = out | replace: '100 % nylon', 'premium nylon'
  assign out = out | replace: '100 % Nylon', 'Premium Nylon'
  assign out = out | replace: '100%nylon', 'premium nylon'
  assign out = out | replace: '100%Nylon', 'Premium Nylon'

  echo out
-%}
